        "expert-title": "AI Assistant",
        "findings-content": "<p>This page structures the main insights from the 671 toponyms left by the d’Entrecasteaux and Baudin expeditions into six sections. Each button opens the detailed page.</p><div class=\"findings-section\"><p><a class=\"resource-primary-link\" href=\"findings-1.html\">1. The d’Entrecasteaux and Baudin voyages of discovery</a></p><p>Two expeditions (1792-1793 and 1800-1804) launched in revolutionary and Napoleonic times: search for La Pérouse, hydrographic survey, scientific collection.</p></div><div class=\"findings-section\"><p><a class=\"resource-primary-link\" href=\"findings-2.html\">2. Earlier French voyages</a></p><p>A century of French exploration toward Terra Australis, with formal instructions, embarked scientists, and precise charting.</p></div><div class=\"findings-section\"><p><a class=\"resource-primary-link\" href=\"findings-3.html\">3. The Right of the first discovery</a></p><p>The right of first discovery clarifies European naming practices and the historical, political, and memorial stakes of French toponyms in Australia.</p></div><div class=\"findings-section\"><p><a class=\"resource-primary-link\" href=\"findings-4.html\">4. D'Entrecasteaux’s cautious choice of nomenclature</a></p><p>Names rooted in the voyage (ships, crew, features) to stay neutral and navigation-focused, with accurate surveys from Beautemps-Beaupré.</p></div><div class=\"findings-section\"><p><a class=\"resource-primary-link\" href=\"findings-5.html\">5. Péron and Freycinet’s nomenclature</a></p><p>Reworked under the Empire: scientists, military and state figures, arts and letters, plus a strong Napoleonic imprint.</p></div><div class=\"findings-section\"><p><a class=\"resource-primary-link\" href=\"findings-6.html\">6. The reception of the nomenclatures</a></p><p>Two contrasting logics (voyage vs. national narrative) largely revised after 1815; more than half of the names are still in use today.</p></div>",
        "findings-page-title": "Findings <a href=\"objet.html\" title=\"Back to Aim\"><img src=\"img/up-arrow.svg\" alt=\"Back to Aim\" style=\"width:24px; vertical-align:middle; margin-left:8px; opacity:0.8;\"></a>",
