        "intro-p1": "More than 670 French place names were assigned along the Australian coastline following the expeditions of d&rsquo;Entrecasteaux (1791&ndash;1794) and Baudin (1800&ndash;1804). Today, around 360 of these names still appear on Australian maps.",
        "intro-p2": "These voyages formed part of a broader effort to improve the geographical knowledge of the coasts of New Holland &mdash; present-day Australia &mdash; at a time when large sections of its shoreline remained imperfectly known to Europeans.",
